Do not ask for the IMS context before the stack's boot sequence has finished

Stock's first IMS request is granted every time. Ours comes back 168 in 9-61 ms
on essentially every boot, and the stack only gets a context on a later
attempt -- which is why both SIMs register around T+68s at best where stock has
them at T+13-14s.

The difference is where the request sits in the boot, not when in wall-clock
time. Measured on identical firmware, from the network becoming known to the
first ims SETUP_DATA_CALL:

    stock  ch 0xf5   6491ms -> 11238ms    4.7s
    stock  ch 0xf6   5974ms -> 11332ms    5.4s
    r52    ch 0xf5   8758ms ->  9429ms    0.7s
    r52    ch 0xf6   8764ms ->  9227ms    0.5s

Stock spends those five seconds finishing the per-stack boot work -- the config
batch, the card reads, the profile pushes, the post-radio-on replay -- and asks
after. We asked as soon as net_registered flipped, part-way through our own.

So the gate is the work, not a delay: the modem reports when a stack's boot
sequence has finished and provisioning waits for that. A faster or slower
device asks whenever its own work is done, which is the portable form of what
stock does rather than a number copied out of this capture.

Because the gate only runs when the modem pushes an access-tech update, a
condition that becomes true in between has to announce itself, so the modem
re-runs it via mm_sit_ims_reevaluate() -- otherwise nothing would start until
the next RAT indication happened to arrive.

I previously reported timing as ruled out, on the grounds that our *retries* at
25 s and 114 s were also refused 168. That was the wrong comparison: a retry
happens after the CP has already refused once, which is not the same state as a
clean first ask. The lead was live and I closed it on bad evidence.

If the first request is granted after this, that was the cause and both SIMs
should register together at around 15 s. If it still comes back 168, timing is
genuinely dead.

The retry-limit test drives the IMS object with no modem behind it, so the
fixture now reports the precondition itself.

